    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (80.98) and **Yordan Alvarez** (79.98) serving as our undisputed pillars. **Pete Crow-Armstrong** presents the highest ceiling on the roster, buoyed by a prime matchup against Arrighetti (xERA 4.97) and a slow opposing delivery that screams stolen base potential\u2014the lifeblood of our strategy. Meanwhile, **Yordan Alvarez** continues to operate in a tier of his own, providing elite xwOBA metrics against Taillon. **Trea Turner** and **Kyle Schwarber** also anchor the lineup with strong scores above 64, benefiting from favorable spots in the batting order and exploitable matchups against Williams. **Dillon Dingler** earns a high grade of 63.89, with his score significantly amplified by a dynamic platoon advantage against Akin that helps him clear the threshold despite a moderate base projection.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision today involved **Chase Meidroth**, who finished just shy of the Zebras' 40.0 floor with a 34.93 score. While he remains a depth piece, the decision to bench him was driven by a brutal matchup against a sub-3.00 xERA arm, which negated his baseline utility. Conversely, we are keeping a close eye on the volatility surrounding **Junior Caminero**; despite a 56.79 score, his matchup against an elite arm like Cole presents the highest risk of a sub-optimal outcome. We have opted to leave **Colt Keith** and **Luke Raley** on the bench today, as both are not currently appearing in the official starting lineup, reinforcing our commitment to maximizing game efficiency by avoiding sub-optimal pinch-hit scenarios. We remain cautious of **Christian Yelich**, whose score (44.82) is heavily suppressed by a negative platoon and a challenging park environment, though his ability to exploit a slow delivery keeps him marginally ahead of the bench options.",
